---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | ShouldISpend"
  description="Read the ShouldISpend privacy policy, including information about cookies, analytics, advertising, usage data, and third-party services."
>
  <style>
    .container {
      max-width: 860px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 80px 24px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      color: var(--accent);
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 2px;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      font-weight: 700;
      margin-bottom: 16px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.8rem, 7vw, 4.5rem);
      line-height: 1;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    h2 {
      font-size: 1.65rem;
      margin: 48px 0 16px;
      color: #0f172a;
    }

    p,
    li {
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      line-height: 1.85;
      color: #334155;
    }

    p {
      margin-bottom: 24px;
    }

    ul {
      padding-left: 24px;
      margin-bottom: 28px;
    }

    li {
      margin-bottom: 12px;
    }

    .updated {
      color: var(--muted);
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      margin-bottom: 36px;
    }

    .callout {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      background: var(--card);
      border-radius: 22px;
      padding: 24px;
      margin: 36px 0;
    }

    .callout p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 768px) {
      .container {
        padding: 64px 22px;
      }

      h1 {
        font-size: 2.5rem;
      }

      p,
      li {
        font-size: 1rem;
      }
    }
  </style>

  <main class="container">
    <div class="eyebrow">Privacy Policy</div>

    <h1>Your Privacy Matters.</h1>

    <p class="updated">
      Last updated: May 23, 2026
    </p>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend is designed to help users evaluate spending decisions,
      financial pressure, savings impact, debt burden, and long-term affordability.
      This privacy policy explains what information may be collected when you use
      the website and how that information may be used.
    </p>

    <p>
  Transparency matters to ShouldISpend. This page is intended to explain, in
  plain language, what information may be collected, how third-party services
  may operate, and what privacy choices visitors have while using the website.
</p>

    <div class="callout">
      <p>
        ShouldISpend calculators are educational tools only and do not require
        user accounts, financial logins, or stored personal financial profiles.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>Information We Do Not Intentionally Collect</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend does not require user accounts, passwords, banking credentials,
      or sensitive financial account access.
    </p>

    <p>
      Calculator entries are intended for temporary educational estimates and are
      not designed to create stored financial profiles for users.
    </p>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend does not intentionally collect personally sensitive financial
      information such as bank account numbers, Social Security numbers, credit
      card numbers, or tax records.
    </p>

    <h2>Analytics and Anonymous Usage Information</h2>

    <p>
      Like many websites, ShouldISpend may collect anonymous or aggregated usage
      information to improve performance, content quality, calculators, navigation,
      and overall user experience.
    </p>

    <p>
      This information may include:
    </p>

    <ul>
      <li>Pages viewed and time spent on pages</li>
      <li>General traffic sources and referral information</li>
      <li>Browser type, operating system, and device type</li>
      <li>Approximate geographic region</li>
      <li>Site interaction patterns and navigation behavior</li>
      <li>General performance and diagnostic information</li>
    </ul>

    <p>
      This information is generally aggregated and not used to personally identify visitors.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies and Similar Technologies</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend may use cookies, local storage, analytics technologies,
      advertising identifiers, or similar tools to improve website functionality,
      understand traffic patterns, measure engagement, and support advertising, analytics, and website functionality.
    </p>

    <p>
      Cookies are small files stored on your device that help websites recognize
      browsers, remember preferences, and improve user experience.
    </p>

    <p>
      You may disable or limit cookies through your browser settings. Some website
      functionality may behave differently if cookies are disabled.
    </p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend may use Google Analytics, including Google Analytics 4 (GA4),
      to measure website traffic and understand how visitors interact with pages,
      calculators, guides, and tools.
    </p>

    <p>
      Google Analytics may collect anonymous usage information through cookies or
      similar technologies. This information helps improve calculator quality,
      page structure, navigation, and user experience.
    </p>

    <p>
      You can learn more about how Google uses information from sites and apps
      that use Google services through Google's privacy resources and available
      opt-out tools.
    </p>

    <h2>Advertising and Google AdSense</h2>

<p>
  ShouldISpend may display advertisements through Google AdSense or other
  third-party advertising partners.
</p>

<p>
  Third-party vendors, including Google, may use cookies, web beacons,
  advertising identifiers, or similar technologies to serve ads based on a
  visitor's prior visits to this website or other websites.
</p>

<p>
  Google's advertising cookies may help:
</p>

<ul>
  <li>Show more relevant advertisements</li>
  <li>Measure advertising performance</li>
  <li>Reduce repetitive ads</li>
  <li>Improve fraud detection and security</li>
  <li>Support analytics and website performance insights</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Visitors may opt out of personalized advertising by visiting
  Google Ad Settings.
</p>

<p>
  Browser settings, privacy tools, and opt-out extensions may also help limit
  certain tracking technologies and advertising personalization.
</p>

    <h2>Affiliate Relationships</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend may include affiliate links or referral partnerships in the future.
      If a visitor clicks certain links and takes qualifying actions, the website may
      earn a commission at no additional cost to the visitor.
    </p>

    <p>
      Any future affiliate relationships are intended to support the operation and
      growth of the site.
    </p>

    <h2>External Websites</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend may link to external websites, products, services, or third-party resources.
      This privacy policy does not apply to external websites, and ShouldISpend is not
      responsible for the privacy practices or content of third-party services.
    </p>

    <h2>Data Retention</h2>

    <p>
      Anonymous analytics and usage information may be retained for reasonable periods
      to help analyze traffic trends, improve calculators, diagnose technical issues,
      and evaluate website performance.
    </p>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend does not currently maintain personal financial profiles tied to
      calculator entries.
    </p>

    <h2>Your Privacy Choices</h2>

    <ul>
      <li>You may disable cookies through your browser settings.</li>
      <li>You may use browser privacy tools or extensions to limit tracking.</li>
      <li>You may manage ad personalization through Google Ad Settings.</li>
      <li>You may choose not to enter information into calculators if preferred.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>California Privacy Notice</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend does not sell personal information in the traditional sense.
      However, some advertising or analytics technologies may be considered data
      sharing under certain privacy regulations.
    </p>

    <p>
      Visitors may limit certain tracking technologies through browser controls,
      privacy tools, and available advertising opt-out settings.
    </p>

    <h2>Children's Privacy</h2>

    <p>
      ShouldISpend is intended for a general audience and is not directed toward
      children under the age of 13. The website does not intentionally collect
      personal information from children.
    </p>

    <h2>Policy Updates</h2>

    <p>
      This privacy policy may be updated periodically as ShouldISpend evolves,
      adds new features, expands advertising services, or introduces additional
      tools and functionality.
    </p>

    <p>
      The "Last updated" date at the top of this page reflects the most recent revision.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>

    <p>
      Questions regarding this privacy policy may be submitted through the
<a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
    </p>
    <section>
      <h2>Related Trust Pages</h2>

      <p>
        For more information about how to use ShouldISpend content, review the
        <a href="/about/">About</a> page, <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>,
        <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>, or contact the site through the
        <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>